    "MINOR: The evaluation plan does not explicitly include K=1 (greedy/beam search) as a named baseline condition. While K=1 is implicitly the floor of the K ∈ {4, 8, 16, 32} sweep, reviewers will want to see 'Standard fine-tune (K=1)' labeled in Table 1 to isolate the contribution of K-sample aggregation from the fine-tuning baseline. Add K=1 as an explicit row.",
